# What must never be uploaded to a build.
#
# The CLI does not apply .gitignore the way the git integration does, so
# `vercel --prod` was packing data/, which holds a 188 MB corpus of the client's own
# mail (data/corpus/sweep-threads.jsonl). It failed with "File size limit exceeded
# (100 MB)" — which is the good outcome; the bad one is a version of that file small
# enough to succeed, quietly shipping client correspondence into a deployment.
#
# THIS LIST MATCHES WHAT .gitignore ALREADY KEEPS OUT, and nothing more. A first
# attempt also excluded scripts/, test/, sim/ and docs/ and the build failed on
# `app/lib/sweepLabelsDb.ts` — it dynamically imports ../../scripts/_corpus.mjs, so
# scripts/ is reachable from app/ and has to ship. A CLI deploy that excludes more
# than the git integration does is a deploy that behaves differently from every
# other deploy, which is worse than a large upload.
#
# (Note for later: that same import reads the 188 MB corpus from disk at RUNTIME.
# The corpus is gitignored, so it has never existed in any deployment — that path
# throws in production today. Not fixed here; see the health sweep.)
data/
.tmp-data/
n8n/backups/
*.log
